Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:34:25 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Iteration 3: model-inferred main issue no longer selects
 the primary route

Team decision (recorded in docs/SPECIFICATION_DISCREPANCIES.md):
- organisationRouting.ts honours main_actionable_issue only when its quoted
  evidence states a priority (STATED_PRIORITY); otherwise the deterministic
  RT08 tie-break applies, so code, not the model, selects the primary
- T20/T21 primary stays Undetermined with all valid routes offered to staff;
  a priority stated in a staff clarification still selects it
- T08 unchanged; recorded as a known model limitation
- tests: inferred vs stated priority, T20, T21, T05 unaffected, no scenario
  narrative states a priority (83 passing)
- offline re-score of 66 recorded real extractions: PASS 45 -> 49,
  MISMATCH 14 -> 10 (docs/live-e2e-report.json regenerated)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
